(footprint "QFN-60_L7.0-W7.0-P0.40-TL-EP3.4_Dense_V4"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Raspberry Pi RP2354A QFN-60 7x7. Land per ${OPENDRONE_LIB}/datasheet/RP2350.pdf (RP2350 Datasheet) s14.1.2 Figure 144 'Recommended PCB Footprint for the RP2350 QFN-60 package' (pdf p1329): pads 0.20 x 0.875 at 0.40 pitch, 7.75 outer / 6.00 inner, EP 3.40; RP2354A uses the same QFN-60 (s14.3); pin 1 top-left, counter-clockwise. Figure 144 land with the toe trimmed (heel edge 3.00 kept); EP and paste as _W. DENSE: budget envelope QFN60_7 7.2 vs Figure 144 7.75: outer edge 3.875 -> 3.70 (0.20 past the 7.0 body, IPC-7351B density L toe, as the RTC6705/SX1280 _Dense lands); pads 0.70 x 0.20. Corrected copy of OpenDrone:QFN-60_L7.0-W7.0-P0.40-TL-EP3.4 (same frame), F.Fab body, no component silk; spec hardware/tools/land_specs/QFN-60_L7.0-W7.0-P0.40-TL-EP3.4_Dense.json | V4 (D95): RP2354A: EP land 3.40 -> 2.40 (50 % of the 3.40 package pad), land holds 2x2 board GND vias 0.35/0.20 at 1.00 (via-in-pad, placed on the board), paste 2x2 0.90 (56 %); QSPI SD0-SD3/SCLK lands 55-59 removed (in-package flash, pins left open); GPIO2/GPIO3 lands 4/5 removed (unused after the D89 IO trim)")
	(tags "Raspberry Pi RP2354A QFN-60 7x7 V4 D95")
